From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:25:13 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: xpon: omci: drop the services of an ANI-side bridge port when it is deleted

A Delete marks the object pending_delete, works the services out again
and only then removes it. omci_agent_resolve_bridge_locked() skips a
UNI-side MAC bridge port that is marked, and the lookups of the mapper,
the GEM interworking TP, the GEM port CTP and the T-CONT do not return a
marked object, but the walk over the ANI-side ports of the bridge took
every stored port. Deleting an ANI-side MAC bridge port configuration
data therefore left its services installed in hardware until some later
Create, Set or Delete of a datapath class worked them out again.

Skip an ANI-side port that is not active, as the UNI side does.

Read in the source in a security review of the OMCI agent.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
@@ -3205,9 +3205,14 @@ omci_agent_resolve_bridge_locked(struct
 		u8 wan_type;
 		unsigned int pcp;
 
+		/*
+		 * A port that is being deleted is still stored, marked, while
+		 * the services are worked out without it.
+		 */
 		if (wan_port->class_id !=
 		    OMCI_CLASS_MAC_BRIDGE_PORT_CONFIG_DATA ||
 		    wan_port == lan_port ||
+		    !omci_mib_object_active(agent, wan_port) ||
 		    get_unaligned_be16(wan_port->data) != bridge_id)
 			continue;
 		wan_type = wan_port->data[3];
